## Authentication
API Key (x-goog-api-key) — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.

### Providing credentials
- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).
- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.

## Dependencies
- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.
- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).

## Endpoints

### Auth Flow (3)
- `GET /s/_/ytmainappweb/_/js/{jToken}/am=aaaaqaaaaam/d=1/br=1/{br=1Token}/m=root_chunk,base_chunk,main_chunk` — Fetch initial Javascript chunks for authentication flow.
- `GET /s/_/ytmainappweb/_/js/{jToken}/am=aaaaqaaaaam/d=1/exm=base_chunk,main_chunk,root_chunk/ed=1/br=1/{br=1Token}/m=x0iwkb` — Fetch additional Javascript chunks for authentication flow.
- `GET /s/_/ytmainappweb/_/ss/{ssToken}/am=aaaaqiaaqam/d=0/br=1/{br=1Token}` — Fetch shared settings for authentication flow.

### Data Read (4)
- `GET /{id}` — Retrieve video or channel details by ID.
- `GET /pagead/interaction` — Report ad interaction events.
- `GET /pcs/activeview` — Report active view events.
- `POST /youtubei/v1/account/get_setting_values` — Retrieve account settings.

### Data Write (2)
- `POST /api/stats/{statId}` — Report statistical data.
- `POST /youtubei/v1/notification_registration/set_registration` — Register or update push notification settings.

### Search (1)
- `GET /s/search/audio/{id}` — Search for audio content by ID.

### Media (1)
- `POST /videoplayback` — Request video playback data.

### Core API (2)
- `POST /api/jnn/v1/generateit` — Generate an IT token (likely for video playback).
- `POST /youtubei/v1/{v1Id}` — Execute a core YouTube API function.

